A class is the container almost everything else hangs off — students, attendance, the timetable
grid, exam results and fee assignments are all addressed by class. Create the class first.

**You need:** access to **Students → Classes**, and permission to create classes.

## Steps

1. Open **Students → Classes** in the side drawer.
2. Select **Add Class**. The **Add New Class** dialog opens.
3. Fill in the four fields:
   - **Grade** — pick from the list. This is what groups classes together for
     [Grade Curriculum](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-grade-curriculum) and for grade-wide reporting,
     so it has to be right.
   - **Syllabus** — pick from the list. Classes on different syllabuses in the same grade are
     reported separately.
   - **Class Name** — required, and this is the class's identifier throughout the system. Short and
     conventional is better than descriptive: `10-A`, `Grade 3 Blue`. It is what you will see in
     every class dropdown from now on.
   - **Teacher Name** — optional. You can leave it empty and set the class teacher properly later.
4. Select **Save**.

You should see **Class added successfully**, and the new class appears in the list. If you get
**Failed to add class.** instead, the most common cause is a class name that already exists.

## Setting the class teacher

The **Teacher Name** field on the dialog is free text — it is a label, not a link to a teacher
record. To actually assign the teacher who owns the class:

1. Open the class from **Students → Classes**.
2. Use the **⋮ More options** menu on the class screen.
3. Choose **Edit Class Teacher** and pick the teacher.

This matters: the class teacher is who gets the class in **My Class**, and who can mark its
attendance. See [Taking Attendance as a Teacher](/docs/educonnect-teacher-taking-attendance).

## What to do next

Once the class exists, in roughly this order:

1. [Add students to it](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student) — one at a time, or
   [import them from Excel](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-import-students).
2. [Assign its subjects](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-class-subjects) so it can be timetabled.
3. Include it in [fee setup](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-fee-setup) if fees differ by class.

